message.content:
Use CSS with the `:hover` pseudo-class on the `span` itself. The `:hover` selector applies to any element, including `span`, so you can change its text color when the mouse is over it.[6][8]

```html
<span class="hover-text">Hover over me</span>

<style>
  .hover-text {
    color: black;
  }

  .hover-text:hover {
    color: red;
  }
</style>
```

If the `span` already has an inline `style="color: ..."` attribute, that inline style can override your stylesheet, so remove the inline styling or use a more specific rule if needed.[1]

If you want, I can also show the same effect using inline CSS only or with a smooth transition.

